      "final_text": "I'll reduce the exponent using Fermat's little theorem first, then square-and-multiply by hand.\n\n**Exponent reduction.** 5557 is prime (trial division up to \u221a5557 \u2248 74 finds no factor), and gcd(7, 5557) = 1, so 7^5556 \u2261 1 (mod 5557). Since 8432 = 5556 + 2876:\n\n7^8432 \u2261 7^2876 (mod 5557).\n\n**Binary of 2876:** 2876 = 2048 + 512 + 256 + 32 + 16 + 8 + 4 = 2^11 + 2^9 + 2^8 + 2^5 + 2^4 + 2^3 + 2^2. So I need 7^(2^k) for k = 2..11 and multiply those together.\n\n**Squaring steps** (each line is the previous value squared, reduced mod 5557; 7^(2^0)=7 is the seed):\n\n- 7^2 \u2261 49\n- 49^2 = 2401 \u2261 **2401** (k=2)\n- 2401^2 = 5,764,801; 5557\u00b71037 = 5,762,609 \u2192 **2192** (k=3)\n- 2192^2 = 4,804,864; 5557\u00b7864 = 4,801,248 \u2192 **3616** (k=4)\n- 3616^2 = 13,075,456; 5557\u00b72352 = 13,070,064 \u2192 **5392** (k=5)\n- 5392 \u2261 \u2212165; (\u2212165)^2 = 27,225; 27,225 \u2212 22,228 \u2192 **4997** (k=6)\n- 4997 \u2261 \u2212560; (\u2212560)^2 = 313,600; 313,600 \u2212 311,192 \u2192 **2408** (k=7)\n- 2408^2 = 5,798,464; 5557\u00b71043 = 5,795,951 \u2192 **2513** (k=8)\n- 2513^2 = 6,315,169; 5557\u00b71136 = 6,312,752 \u2192 **2417** (k=9)\n- 2417^2 = 5,841,889; 5557\u00b71051 = 5,840,407 \u2192 **1482** (k=10)\n- 1482^2 = 2,196,324; 5557\u00b7395 = 2,195,015 \u2192 **1309** (k=11)\n\n**Multiply the needed factors** (k = 11, 9, 8, 5, 4, 3, 2), reducing mod 5557 each step:\n\n- 1309 \u00b7 2417 = 3,163,853; 5557\u00b7569 = 3,161,933 \u2192 **1920**\n- 1920 \u00b7 2513 = 4,824,960; 5557\u00b7868 = 4,823,476 \u2192 **1484**\n- 1484 \u00b7 5392 \u2261 1484\u00b7(\u2212165) = \u2212244,860 \u2261 \u2212352 \u2192 **5205**\n- 5205 \u00b7 3616 \u2261 (\u2212352)\u00b73616 = \u22121,272,832 \u2261 \u2212279 \u2192 **5278**\n- 5278 \u00b7 2192 \u2261 (\u2212279)\u00b72192 = \u2212611,568 \u2261 \u2212298 \u2192 **5259**\n- 5259 \u00b7 2401 \u2261 (\u2212298)\u00b72401 = \u2212715,498 \u2261 \u22124202 \u2192 **1355**\n\n1355"
